{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider 64 send 0xa5 failed as TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0x01 want 0xa5 with tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause in excerpt is line 46 reg [2:0] send_bitcnt which cannot hold the 10-bit send_pattern frame (line 45), truncating 10 to 2 and corrupting TX plus reg_dat_wait at line 52. Wiring per picosoc/simpleuart.v:20 and picosoc/picosoc.v:201, picosoc/picosoc.v:204 shows reg_dat_we/do path used for this loopback.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 	reg [9:0] send_pattern;
-	reg [2:0] send_bitcnt;
+	reg [3:0] send_bitcnt;
 	reg [31:0] send_divcnt;
 	reg send_dummy;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP: uart data mismatch, loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

